/", -0.0007094276370480657], ["/C", -8.24595832824707]]}, {"t": "C", "lp": -0.0005681340117007494, "top": [["C", -0.0005681340117007494], ["CC", -8.403091430664062]]}, {"t": "++", "lp": -0.018307657912373543, "top": [["++", -0.018307657912373543], [" compiler", -4.13619327545166]]}, {"t": " Compiler", "lp": -0.3355174660682678, "top": [[" Compiler", -0.3355174660682678], [" compiler", -1.2707171440124512]]}, {"t": " for", "lp": -0.571360170841217, "top": [[" for", -0.571360170841217], [" (", -0.8348737359046936]]}, {"t": " C", "lp": -0.05672017112374306, "top": [[" C", -0.05672017112374306], [" **", -2.9021048545837402]]}, {"t": "\n", "lp": -0.6442868113517761, "top": [["\n", -0.6442868113517761], [" code", -0.7665478587150574]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function: Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (compiler paths, library paths, etc.). The `--force` flag forces the environment to be set up even if it appears already configured. Without this, `icx`/`icpx` wouldn't be found.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nThis makes the script exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero status (an error). This is standard practice in build functions to catch failures early.\n\n## The CMake Invocation\n\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja\n```\n- `-S` : source directory (where the CMakeLists.txt lives)\n- `-B` : build directory (where build artifacts go)\n- `-G Ninja` : use the **Ninja** build generator (fast, efficient build system) instead of the default Makefiles\n\n## CMake Configuration Flags\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\n```\nOptimized build with performance optimizations enabled (`-O3`, etc.) and no debug symbols.\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib\n```\n- Install prefix: `/usr` (standard system location)\n- Library directory: `lib` (not `lib64`, which some distros use)\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icx -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=icpx\n```\nUse Intel's compilers:\n- **`icx`** : Intel oneAPI DPC++/C++ Compiler for C\n"}